WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:02.734
It pains me to say,
but I've recently arrived

00:00:02.734 --> 00:00:03.801
at two conclusions
about myself --

00:00:03.801 --> 00:00:07.067
I am not young,
and I am not hip.

00:00:07.067 --> 00:00:08.033
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:09.300
No, it's true.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:11.434
I mean, I can make
a Cobain joke.

00:00:11.434 --> 00:00:14.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:17.200
And because I'm not
young and hip,

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.667
I often don't know how to feel
about some of the things

00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:21.033
that are going on in
our popular culture.

00:00:21.033 --> 00:00:22.033
But fortunately for all of us,

00:00:22.033 --> 00:00:23.434
I do have people
on my writing staff

00:00:23.434 --> 00:00:26.234
who are both of those things,
and nobody on our staff

00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:29.000
is younger and hipper than our
good friend, Jeff Wright.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.501
-Thank you, Seth.

00:00:30.501 --> 00:00:31.834
It's a pleasure to be here,

00:00:31.834 --> 00:00:33.667
and also,
nobody says "hipper" anymore.

00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:35.834
-Oh, really? What do they say?

00:00:35.834 --> 00:00:36.968
-Just "young."
-Okay.

00:00:36.968 --> 00:00:38.267
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.267 --> 00:00:40.501
And just to be completely fair,
we've also invited

00:00:40.501 --> 00:00:43.033
Jeff Wright's counterpart
to join this discussion.

00:00:43.033 --> 00:00:45.133
Please also welcome Jeff Wrong.

00:00:45.133 --> 00:00:46.267
-Hey, Seth!

00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:47.734
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.734 --> 00:00:48.767
Thanks for having me.

00:00:48.767 --> 00:00:50.534
People don't just say "young."

00:00:50.534 --> 00:00:53.534
We say "young and splaaaa."

00:00:53.534 --> 00:00:55.000
-I probably won't.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:56.334
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.334 --> 00:00:57.801
Alright, let's get
down to business.

00:00:57.801 --> 00:01:00.133
After being indicted
on racketeering charges,

00:01:00.133 --> 00:01:02.234
Grammy-winning rapper
Young Thug's lyrics

00:01:02.234 --> 00:01:03.834
are being cited as evidence

00:01:03.834 --> 00:01:06.434
in the sweeping, 56-count
gang indictment,

00:01:06.434 --> 00:01:08.534
again raising a debate
over whether lyrics

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:09.834
are protected free speech.

00:01:09.834 --> 00:01:11.667
Jeff Wright,
what are your thoughts?

00:01:11.667 --> 00:01:13.734
-I think it's unfair, Seth.

00:01:13.734 --> 00:01:15.601
As much as we enjoy raps

00:01:15.601 --> 00:01:18.434
about money, cars,
and unpaid child support,

00:01:18.434 --> 00:01:22.734
a lot of it is just fabricated
and meant for entertainment.

00:01:22.734 --> 00:01:24.400
It's not intended to be real.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:26.667
Except maybe the unpaid
child support part.

00:01:26.667 --> 00:01:27.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.734 --> 00:01:29.567
And we don't do this
to pop music.

00:01:29.567 --> 00:01:32.334
I mean, Bruno Mars said
he'll catch a grenade.

00:01:32.334 --> 00:01:34.567
That doesn't mean he wants
to be sent to war.

00:01:34.567 --> 00:01:36.734
-Right. That is a fair point.

00:01:36.734 --> 00:01:38.734
Jeff Wrong, your thoughts?

00:01:38.734 --> 00:01:40.434
-Fair?

00:01:40.434 --> 00:01:43.334
We should be holding everyone
responsible for their lyrics!

00:01:43.334 --> 00:01:45.501
Foster the People said
in a song,

00:01:45.501 --> 00:01:47.901
"run, run, run,
and outrun his gun."

00:01:47.901 --> 00:01:48.934
Lock them up!

00:01:48.934 --> 00:01:49.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.934 --> 00:01:51.534
Justin Bieber said
in a song that

00:01:51.534 --> 00:01:53.801
he gets his weed from
California.

00:01:53.801 --> 00:01:56.501
Sounds like drug trafficking
to me, Seth.

00:01:56.501 --> 00:01:57.567
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.567 --> 00:01:58.968
Lock him up!

00:01:58.968 --> 00:02:02.667
Freddie Mercury put in a song,
"Mama, just killed a man,"

00:02:02.667 --> 00:02:04.734
and he told everyone
how he did it.

00:02:04.734 --> 00:02:07.100
Lock him up!

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:11.734
And lock his mama up, too,
for not reporting it.

00:02:11.734 --> 00:02:13.300
-Freddie Mercury is dead,
though.

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:16.367
-Well, that's what happens
when you go out

00:02:16.367 --> 00:02:17.701
and just kill a guy!

00:02:17.701 --> 00:02:18.801
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.801 --> 00:02:20.367
There's gonna be some blowback.
-Okay.

00:02:20.367 --> 00:02:22.834
I see why they call you
Jeff Wrong.

00:02:22.834 --> 00:02:24.467
In other news,

00:02:24.467 --> 00:02:26.100
Kourtney Kardashian
and Travis Barker

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:26.934
got married in Italy.

00:02:26.934 --> 00:02:27.934
Jeff Wright, your thoughts?

00:02:27.934 --> 00:02:30.033
-Hey, I am happy for them, Seth.

00:02:30.033 --> 00:02:31.334
Love is in the air.

00:02:31.334 --> 00:02:33.267
However, it was
their third wedding,

00:02:33.267 --> 00:02:34.701
and it's a little bit crazy
to be even

00:02:34.701 --> 00:02:36.701
having one wedding
during COVID.

00:02:36.701 --> 00:02:39.000
I just hope everyone
was vaxxed and boosted.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.334
-Yeah, I didn't think
about it that way.

00:02:40.334 --> 00:02:42.534
It is a little irresponsible
to have three weddings.

00:02:42.534 --> 00:02:43.734
But you gotta be happy for them.

00:02:43.734 --> 00:02:44.801
Jeff Wrong?

00:02:44.801 --> 00:02:46.067
-No, you don't.

00:02:46.067 --> 00:02:47.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:48.968
Boo! We get it.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.734
They love each other.

00:02:50.734 --> 00:02:53.968
But why would you even have
a wedding in Italy

00:02:53.968 --> 00:02:57.200
and have Andrea Bocelli perform

00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:01.567
and have all these cool
celebrities come out with you?

00:03:01.567 --> 00:03:02.801
-I don't know, Jeff Wrong.

00:03:02.801 --> 00:03:05.133
You sound a little bit more like
Jeff Jealous.

00:03:05.133 --> 00:03:07.067
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.067 --> 00:03:09.100
-I'm -- I'm not jealous.
You're jealous.

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:10.534
-Mm. Very mature.

00:03:10.534 --> 00:03:12.734
Alright, lastly, after
a physical altercation

00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:15.734
on a plane, Mike Tyson will not
face any criminal charges.

00:03:15.734 --> 00:03:17.868
-And he shouldn't face
any charges.

00:03:17.868 --> 00:03:21.400
I think he should find the guy
and beat his ass again.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:24.367
-Now, wait a minute,
that opinion sounds wrong,

00:03:24.367 --> 00:03:25.834
but you're Jeff Wright.

00:03:25.834 --> 00:03:28.467
-Yes, because that opinion
is right.

00:03:28.467 --> 00:03:31.934
Look, we all know what that guy
said to Tyson.

00:03:31.934 --> 00:03:36.000
But if you're dumb enough to say
anything to Mike Tyson

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:39.334
in an enclosed space
like an airplane,

00:03:39.334 --> 00:03:42.567
you probably deserve
a punch in the mouth.

00:03:42.567 --> 00:03:43.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.734 --> 00:03:46.000
Plus, now that guy has a story
he can tell

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:47.467
for the rest of his life.

00:03:47.467 --> 00:03:50.534
-You make a compelling point.
Jeff Wrong?

00:03:50.534 --> 00:03:52.567
-Hey, well,

00:03:52.567 --> 00:03:54.501
he said what I was gonna say.

00:03:54.501 --> 00:03:56.167
-Who did?

00:03:56.167 --> 00:03:57.667
-I guess I did, Seth.

00:03:57.667 --> 00:03:59.868
-Well, do you apologize to
Jeff Wrong?

00:03:59.868 --> 00:04:02.000
-I mean...I'm sorry,
Jeff Wrong.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:04.367
-And do you accept his apology?

00:04:04.367 --> 00:04:07.868
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.868 --> 00:04:09.367
-[ Laughing ]

00:04:09.367 --> 00:04:11.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.534 --> 00:04:14.133
It's a simple question.
Do you accept his apology?

00:04:14.133 --> 00:04:16.434
-I...Yeah. It's all good.

00:04:16.434 --> 00:04:18.968
I mean, I might punch him
in the face.

00:04:18.968 --> 00:04:21.367
-Alright. Jeff Wright, final
thoughts, Jeff Wright?

00:04:21.367 --> 00:04:22.901
-Yeah.
-Final thoughts.

00:04:22.901 --> 00:04:24.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.601 --> 00:04:25.767
-Hey --
-No, actually, you know what?

00:04:25.767 --> 00:04:27.267
We have to go on with the show.

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:28.267
But thank you so much,
Jeff Wrong.

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:29.567
Goodbye, Jeff Wrong.

00:04:29.567 --> 00:04:31.133
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.133 --> 00:04:33.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:33.067 --> 00:04:34.133
Jeff Wright and Jeff Wrong,
everybody.

00:04:34.133 --> 00:04:35.133
We'll be right back.

